-- DISI rollback of Migration 056 (international benchmark: the 2019 class).
-- database/release/sql/rollback-056.sql, generated by database/research/056/build.mjs from the same research files as the migration.
--
-- Use only if a production failure requires it. One transaction, guarded. It removes exactly what 056 added - the 2019 benchmark players,
-- signings, population members and population, the 056 rankings, the 056 outcome audits, outcomes and evidence - restores the stored 041 model
-- evaluation rows exactly as 055 wrote them, and refreshes the product snapshots once. The source rows stay as provenance. The listed Dodgers
-- signing (Luis Rodriguez) was never written by 056, so nothing of his is touched; that is proved below.
--
-- The 026 evaluation guard seals ACTIVE rankings (a sealed point-in-time observation is never deleted by research). Restoring the exact
-- pre-056 state is the one sanctioned exception, as in rollback-050 and rollback-055: inside this transaction only, the two guard triggers are
-- disabled, exactly the 056 rankings are removed, and the triggers are enabled again before commit (proved below). 056 can be applied again.

